==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|what}} + {{term|soever}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌwɒtsəʊˈɛvə(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌwʌtsoʊˈɛvɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-whatsoever.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛvə(r)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[whatever|Whatever]].
#* {{w|John Milton}}
#*: In '''whatsoever''' shape he lurk.
#* The Holy Bible, Genesis xxxi. 16
#*: '''Whatsoever''' God hath said unto thee, do.
# In any way; [[at all]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1898|author={{w|Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill}}
|title={{w|The Celebrity}}|chapter=1
|passage=In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius '''whatsoever'''. He never read me any of his manuscripts,&nbsp;[&hellip;], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned.}}
#: {{usex|He gave me no answer '''whatsoever'''.|lang=en}}

